; Snowfield — NEW TerrainDefinition (habitat-tiers ruling, 2026-09-04 -> task-8-brief.md).
; VALUES BELOW ARE A PROPOSAL AWAITING HUMAN SIGN-OFF (same posture as every other
; terrain's cost/scale/model choices in this codebase; see barn.tres for the same
; convention on the buildings side).
;
; WHY IT EXISTS: Husky habitat — the roster's first cold-climate species needs a `snow`
; tag source, and no terrain emitted it before this task.
;
; emitted_tags = ["snow"] is DECIDED by the habitat-tiers ruling (task-8-brief.md's table).
; No radius, no weight, no threshold — the v1 tag model (-> D-25) applies unchanged.
;
; SNOWFIELD MAY BORDER GRASS — human ruling (spec OQ-E): the game is not restricted to
; real-world climate adjacency. This schema entry deliberately carries no placement
; restriction, allowed-neighbour list, or climate gate, and none should be added here.
;
; cost = 0 — natural terrain, "nature is free" (terrain.md's one pricing rule, unchanged by
; this task).
;
; MODEL_SCENE: Snowfield.tscn (CC0, Ultimate Nature Pack's dedicated snow variant set) —
; see that scene's own header for full sourcing/scale detail. Single variant; a
; multi-variant look-pass is out of scope here, same posture Grass/Rock/Wild grass all
; started with before their own later passes.
;
; PLAYER-VISIBLE CONSEQUENCE: Snowfield is a new, free-to-paint entry in the Terraform
; palette — flagged prominently per this task's brief, not buried in a count bump.
;
; No `fact_text` copy yet — Content Pipeline step 5 (Content Writer), explicitly out of
; scope for this task.
